Read only the GFileInfo attributes an info carries; no deprecated CSS; detach
a file menu only while it is attached.

GLib reports a getter called for an attribute the info does not carry as a
critical error ("GFileInfo created without standard::size").  The infos of
libfm's virtual folders -- menu://applications/, which the side pane lists as
"Applications", and search:// -- carry a reduced set (no edit name, size,
symlink or backup flag; directories no content type), so opening the file
manager printed a screenful of these.  fm_file_info_set_from_g_file_data(),
the path entry's completion and the display-name walk of the file info job
now ask whether an attribute is there before reading it.

The tab close button's CSS named focus-padding and focus-line-width, style
properties GTK 3 no longer reads and warns about when parsing; the same
intent -- no focus ring around the button -- is outline-width and
outline-offset now.

fm_file_menu_destroy() detached the menu unconditionally, and GTK warns when
a menu that is no longer attached (its window went first) is detached again.

